Funtion app service --> We run small pieces of code that execute when triggered by an event, HTTP request, timer, or message.
Azure Function App is a serverless compute service used to execute small pieces of code based on specific events or triggers
We don't need to maintain servers or continuously run an application.


How does it work?
For example, suppose we want to send an email whenever a new customer registers.
A customer registers.
An event or message is generated.
Azure Function gets triggered.
Function executes the code.
An email is sent to the customer.
Function execution completes.

Common triggers
HTTP Trigger – Executes when an HTTP request is received.
Timer Trigger – Executes at a scheduled time.
Queue Trigger – Executes when a message arrives in a queue.
Blob Trigger – Executes when a blob is created or updated.
Event Hub Trigger – Executes when events arrive in Event Hubs.
Real-time example: Suppose an application uploads invoices to Azure Blob Storage. Whenever a new invoice is uploaded, an Azure Function automatically triggers, processes the invoice, and stores the result in a database.


